{"path":"numeric/complex/atan","title":"std::atan(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>atan<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::complex)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/atan","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes complex arc tangent of a complex value z. Branch cut exists outside the interval [−i, +i] along the imaginary axis.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br>complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> atan<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes complex arc tangent of a complex value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>. Branch cut exists outside the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−i, +i]</span> along the imaginary axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, complex arc tangent of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−π/2, +π/2]</span> along the real axis.\n</p><p>Errors and special cases are handled as if the operation is implemented by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span><code>&nbsp;</code><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/atanh\"><code>std::atanh</code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> z<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, where <code>i</code> is the imaginary unit.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Inverse tangent (or arc tangent) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane. The branch cut is conventionally placed at the line segments <span class=\"texhtml\">(-∞i,-i)</span> and <span class=\"texhtml\">(+i,+∞i)</span> of the imaginary axis.\n</p>\nThe mathematical definition of the principal value of inverse tangent is <span class=\"texhtml\">atan z = -<span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td></tr></table></span> i [ln(1 - iz) - ln (1 + iz)]</span>.\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z1<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"atan\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\"><span class=\"kw1346\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atan</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z1<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"atan\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (the other side of the cut) = \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\"><span class=\"kw1346\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atan</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z3<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/INFINITY\"><span class=\"kw1385\">INFINITY</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"2 * atan\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z3 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\"><span class=\"kw1346\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atan</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>atan(0.000000,2.000000) = (1.570796,0.549306)\natan(-0.000000,2.000000) (the other side of the cut) = (-1.570796,0.549306)\n2 * atan(0.000000,inf) = (3.141593,0.000000)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/asin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>asin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc sine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arcsin{z}}\">arcsin(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/acos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>acos<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc cosine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arccos{z}}\">arccos(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/tan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes tangent of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\tan{z}}\">tan(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan</span><span>atanf</span><span>atanl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc tangent (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arctan{x}}\">arctan(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/atan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\">std::atan</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/catan\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>catan</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::atan(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Computes complex arc tangent of a complex value z."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, complex arc tangent of z is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval [−π/2, +π/2] along…"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Inverse tangent (or arc tangent) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"asin(std::complex)","note":"computes arc sine of a complex number (arcsin(z))"},{"label":"acos(std::complex)","note":"computes arc cosine of a complex number (arccos(z))"},{"label":"tan(std::complex)","note":"computes tangent of a complex number (tan(z))"},{"label":"atan, atanf, atanl","note":"computes arc tangent (arctan(x))"},{"label":"atan(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::atan to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":306,"codeBlockCount":2}
